From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:23:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: sign in with a token, password or QR code, and
 reconnect by re-login

* Sign in with a token password or by QR code

The webOS account UI stores the credential as the account password and
cannot set the "token" protocol option.

- Use the password as the auth token when no token is stored, except
  for the "QRLOGIN" password, which starts the QR code login. A token
  saved by an earlier QR login is reused, so the QR code is only needed
  once; the 4004 handler clears it when it is revoked.
- Render the QR code as a PNG (zlib is already linked) instead of TGA,
  so the account UI can show it inline, and pass the account to
  purple_request_fields so the transport can route it.
- With no request UI, post a plain-text explanation instead of the
  inline image and ASCII QR code, which the Messaging app cannot show.

qrcode_tga_output is no longer called, so mark it G_GNUC_UNUSED. The
helpers that wrote the PNG to /media/internal and launched a separate
viewer app through luna-send were already unused (the account UI shows
the QR code inline now) and are not carried here.

* Hand a remote-auth captcha to the account UI

Discord can require an hCaptcha before it exchanges a QR login ticket
for a token. The response then carries captcha_sitekey, captcha_rqdata
and captcha_rqtoken instead of encrypted_token.

Show these through purple_request_fields, with an editable
"captcha_key" field. The webOS account UI solves the captcha in a web
view and returns the response token in that field; the plugin then
posts remote-auth/login again with the ticket, captcha_key and
captcha_rqtoken. Give up after three captchas in a row. A UI without
request fields gets a connection error saying the captcha cannot be
shown.

* Reconnect through a full re-login

The in-place reconnects (OP_RECONNECT, the five minute restart,
websocket close and lost connection) call discord_start_socket on the
existing DiscordAccount. When the transport has closed the account in
between, the hash tables are gone, and the reconnected account logs
GLib criticals and cannot send or sync.

Report a network error instead, so the webOS transport closes the
account and logs in again with fresh state. As a safety net,
discord_start_socket also recreates any table a close has freed.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
---
